+# Codex reflection
+
+Read [codex-tools.md](codex-tools.md) for tool and instruction mapping.
+
+Use a transcript only if this runtime explicitly supplies the current session's
+path and its format can be read. Do not run the Claude JSONL finder on Codex logs
+or search the user's session store. Otherwise prepare a digest of this
+conversation with the user's corrections, decisions, tool evidence, and skills
+actually loaded. State that the review used a digest.
+
+Use the available `spawn_agent` and wait tools. Pass each reviewer its template
+and the same transcript or digest. Use the configured session model by default;
+only use model overrides the user requested and the runtime supports. Do not
+pass Claude model slugs or Claude `subagent_type` fields. Follow the tool schema
+for context isolation and retain available MCP access.
+
+Use `skill-creator` for substantive skill edits when available; otherwise use
+this collection's `writing-skills`. Do not call an absent plugin-dev skill.
